<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Kloof Sept qtr pre-capex net profit slips.</title>
<headline>Kloof Sept qtr pre-capex net profit slips.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter to end-Sept versus preceding quarter</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit before capital spending	 93.99 vs 118.72</p>
<p>    Capital spending				 66.85 vs  81.61</p>
<p> output (kg)</p>
<p>    Kloof-					  5,753.0 vs 6,359.9</p>
<p>    Leeudoorn-				    1,447.1 vs 1,544.3</p>
<p>    Libanon-					2,028.5 vs 1,973.5</p>
<p>Tonnes milled/treated</p>
<p>    Kloof-					  481,000 vs 487,000</p>
<p>    Leeudoorn-				    286,000 vs 338,000</p>
<p>    Libanon-					408,000 vs 409,000</p>
<p>Yield (gram/t)</p>
<p>    Kloof-					     12.0 vs    13.1</p>
<p>    Leeudoorn-					  5.1 vs     4.6</p>
<p>    Libanon-					    5.0 vs     4.8</p>
<p>Cost (rand/kg)</p>
<p>    Kloof-					   35,421 vs 30,478</p>
<p>    Leeudoorn-				     66,383 vs 65,214</p>
<p>    Libanon-					 57,713 vs 58,331</p>
<p>Revenue (rand/kg)</p>
<p>    Kloof-					   55,441 vs 53,921</p>
<p>    Leeudoorn-				     55,324 vs 53,607</p>
<p>    Libanon-					 55,401 vs 53,904</p>
<p>    Full name: Kloof Gold Mining Co Ltd, managed by Gold Fields</p>
<p>of South Africa Ltd</p>
<p>     NOTE - The company said that the tonnage milled was expected</p>
<p>to increase in the forthcoming quarter and gold yield was</p>
<p>expected to improve slightly. (c) Reuters Limited 1996</p>
</text>
